 "definitions": {
  "edges": "DATA edge = (def point, use point) from the `d` facts, def != use; CONTROLLED_BY edge = (point, cond) from the `cb` facts with CDG self-edges dropped and (point, cond) pairs de-duplicated (-spec2 §1.4 G-4).",
  "join": "param by spec index (the name is only a sanity diagnostic); ret by ordinal (line must equal the label's, else the unique ret on the label's line); call by (calleeName, ordinal) when that call site is on the label's line, else the unique call site of that calleeName on the label's line (tag `ordinalShift`), else unresolved; cond by line and collapsed code (equal, else equal ignoring all whitespace [Joern re-spaces `(int, float)` as `(int,float)`], else one contains the other, on that line; several candidates at the same tier = unresolved).  A pair with an unresolved endpoint is a miss, listed as `endpoint-unresolved`.",
  "paramIndex": "spec index = Joern index - 1 after dropping the implicit `this` (index 0, named `this`) for javascript, java, csharp and cpp; python: Joern index 0 (self/cls) is -1, then index - 1; go: Joern index 0 (the receiver) is -1, then index - 1; a C# extension-method `this` parameter (Joern code starts `this `) is -1 and the rest count from 0.",
  "points": "Points per method are those of bundle spec §5.4-§5.6 as normalize.py derives them: param (index), ret (ordinal over the method's own RETURNs sorted by line, column, id), cond (every CDG source), callsite (callee name + ordinal over same-name call sites sorted by the position of the callee's last identifier, found in the SOURCE from the call's start; a call whose name never occurs in the source is synthetic and is not a point, and an edge touching it is dropped, as normalize.py drops it).",
  "strata": "convention:* = the Part F audit's `convention` tag on a VALID decision (adjudication/<lang>-flow-audit.jsonl), joined to the final pair by (ordinal, kind, endpoint ids without line); provenance:* = the final-set provenance field; frontend-default-ignored-dir = labelled methods whose path has a directory segment the shipped frontend ignores by default (report §a1.4)"
 },
